#: ../../webgis-src/chb2_using-mapserver/sec05_two-layers/section.rst:91
msgid ""
"Here is an explanation of why this is done. If we continue to add layers "
"on top of the state layer, the contours are most likely to be masked by "
"these layers. To be able to see the borders and add other layers, we have"
" to separate the borders layer from the state polygon layer and place it "
"on top of the other other layers. There is an order in how to define/add "
"layers, which will be explained later. Here you just need to remember "
"according to “Later on top” (layers defined later will be displayed on "
"the top)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb2_using-mapserver/sec06_multiple-layers/section.rst:4
msgid "Build a map with multiple layers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb2_using-mapserver/sec06_multiple-layers/section.rst:6
msgid ""
"MapServer builds maps by stacking layers together. On every render, it is"
" placed at the top of the stack. Each layer displays features selected "
"from a single dataset. Features to display can be selected using Unix "
"regular expressions, string comparisons and logical expressions. You can "
"think of layers as topics due to the similarity of data and the "
"similarity of style parameters such as scale, color, and labels. The "
"display of layers is under interactive control, allowing the user to "
"select which layers to render. While it is not possible to generate "
"layers dynamically, it is possible to populate empty layers with dynamic "
"data and manipulate them via URL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb2_using-mapserver/sec06_multiple-layers/section.rst:22
msgid ""
"To make the map richer, continue adding new data (river data) using a new"
" ``LAYER`` object. The definitions of each layer are relatively "
"independent and have nothing to do with each other."
msgstr ""

